{
  "format": "supersilvia-workspace",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "A spectrum ring",
  "kind": "video",
  "blurb": "The sound in thirty-six bands, a rainbow bar each round a ring",
  "layout": "linear",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "slug": "note",
      "pos": {
        "x": 40.0,
        "y": 40.0
      },
      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "First choose a sound in the Main Input panel on the left, under Audio: a microphone, a Sound file, or System audio (what you hear). The Main Input's Spectrum is a list of 128 levels from low to high. Bands gathers it into thirty-six, Lag lets each fall slowly, and Multiply and Add make a band a bar's Scale Y, so even silence leaves a ring of short dashes. A Range of turns stands each bar out from the middle, and a Range into an HSLA's Hue colors them red round to violet. Try Bands' Count, Low and High, or Lag's Fall at 1."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
